import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 647 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 648 | 2026-10-24 | **Scales and Key signatures in the Lesson Book's feel, the butler at the bottom; the tag says LESSON (her calls).** A lesson with a book page now opens with the page (title, words, printed picture, the butler's Remember line), then its 'The words' and 'At the piano' one by one; the last step, 'On the keys →', opens the keyboard lesson the Home already had (with '← The book page' to go back and the butler under it). Scales, in the book's order: The major scale (sc-shape), C major fingering (sc-wr), White keys: left hand, Scale degrees (sc-deg), G major and F major (sc-same, both pages), then black keys, both hands, all twelve, chromatic, minor, pentatonic. Key signatures: The key signature (kf-what), new G major and F major (book pages 3-4; questions: which note it changes, which line it sits on, which finger plays F♯ / B♭), new Key signature and accidental (page 5; how long each lasts, the natural until the bar line), new D major and B♭ major (page 6; count the signs and name the key), then sharp order ... transposing. A keyboard lesson with no book page keeps its screens and gets the butler under it with its own key sentence. The coral tag on a Home lesson says LESSON / 레슨; a tool inside a lesson has no second tag. Also: the lesson engine's last step can lead on (onLast); a book lesson can span two pages; Korean after 샵 fixed app-wide (샵은, 샵을, 샵으로, 샵이, 샵과). **Flag for her:** the butler lines I wrote from each lesson's own words (sc-wl, sc-br, sc-bl, sc-both, sc-all, sc-chrom, sc-min, sc-penta, kf-sharps ... kf-trans), and 'each step round the circle adds one sharp, or one flat'. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/{patch670.py,kq.jsx,lbh.jsx}. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
